Bandai¨ Power Rangersª DatazordsSYSTEM REQUIREMENTSMinimum requirements¥ Macintosh¨ with PowerPCª processor¥ MacOS¨ 7.1 or later¥ 16MB available memory¥ 20MB available hard disk space¥ Monitor capable of displaying 256 colors at 640x480 pixels¥ CD-ROM driveRecommended for improved performance¥ 180 MHz or faster PowerPCª, G3 or G4 processor¥ 32 MB available memory¥ 8X or faster CD-ROM drive¥ Accelerated graphics card¥ High-quality headphones or external loudspeakersSTARTING THE PROGRAMBandai¨ Power Rangersª Datazords does not require an initial installation process.  To start the program:1.  Start your computer.2.  Make sure you have an appropriate system configuration (see above).  For best results, quit any other open applications and turn off or disable any unnecessary system extensions, such as File Sharing and Virtual Memory.3.  Insert the CD into the computer's CD tray.4.  The program will automatically start if QuickTimeª 3.0 or later is installed on your computer and the CD-ROM AutoPlay option is enabled.  If this is not the case, simply locate the CD window that opens up on your desktop and double-click the Datazords icon to start the program.  During startup, the program will automatically set your monitor's color depth to 256 colors (if necessary), and restore your original settings when you quit the program.GAME CONTROLSKeyboard mapTo display a map of the keys assigned to the various Datazord components, click the green Info button at the bottom of the screen.  To return to the Datazord, click anywhere on the screen or press any key.You can also display the keyboard map by pressing Command-I.Volume ControlThe program offers four volume settings: low, medium, high and mute.  To cycle through these settings, click the green Speaker button at the bottom of the screen.You can also adjust the volume by pressing Command-V.Datazord ShutdownTo quit the program, click the Datazord Shutdown button (green cross) at the bottom of the screen.  You will be asked to confirm this action.You can also quit the program by pressing Command-Q or the Escape key.DATAZORD AVAILABILITYEach Power Rangersª action figure ships with its own, custom Datazord CD.  However, as you purchase additional action figures and run their Datazord CDs, the program will enable the corresponding Datazords and allow you to access them from any of the CDs you received.In addition, if you have purchased three or more action figures, the program will automatically enable the MegaDatazord.GAMEPLAYEach Datazord features a wide variety of animated components which can be triggered by clicking on the screen or using the keyboard (see 'Keyboard Map' above).  Most components have several states, so be sure to click on each component several times!Sometimes a component cannot be triggered while it is completing its current animation, or if too many other components are already running.  If this happens, simply wait a few moments for some of the components to return to their resting state.If a component can be triggered, a bold crosshair cursor will appear when you move the mouse over it.Each Datazord also provides several alternate sets of components that can be displayed by clicking the circular red button at the bottom right corner of certain panels.  To return to the original panel, click the red button again.If you have purchased several action figures and started their Datazord CDs, you will be able to switch between several Datazord screens.  To switch to a different Datazord, click the corresponding colored button in the bottom left region of the screen.__________Bandai is a registered trademark and Power Rangers is a trademark of Bandai America, Inc.  Macintosh and MacOS are registered trademarks and QuickTime is a trademark of Apple Computer, Inc.  PowerPC is a trademark of International Business machines Corporation. 